cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If tubebench helps your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "tubebench: four-microphone impedance-tube measurements in MATLAB"
abstract: >-
  tubebench drives a signal generator and a multichannel acquisition module, records four
  microphones around a specimen in an impedance tube and computes the specimen's acoustic
  properties after ASTM E2611 (reflection and transmission coefficients, transmission loss,
  thin-element transfer impedance and the two-port transfer matrix, also from two loads), with a
  validity verdict for every frequency line. It includes a complete virtual tube, so every
  feature, the window included, also runs without hardware. MATLAB R2022b and the Signal
  Processing Toolbox.
authors:
  - family-names: Kim
    given-names: Woongji
version: 1.6.3
date-released: 2026-11-06
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/kimwoongji/tubebench"
keywords:
  - acoustics
  - impedance tube
  - transmission loss
  - transfer matrix
  - transfer impedance
  - ASTM E2611
  - four-microphone method
  - MATLAB
